,\\,}}\n$$" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430667 1072 #uuid "ecc4c2b5-f2f1-588a-9d0e-40046352c05f" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430667 1074 "The given expression is\n\n$$\n(2\\,÷\\,3)\\times (9\\,÷\\,5).\n$$\n\nSince our expression contains multiplication and division only, we can write an equivalent expression by swapping the $÷\\,3$ and the $÷\\,5$:\n\n$$\n(2\\,÷\\,5)\\times (9\\,÷\\,3)\n$$\n\nWe can now interpret the divisions as fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}\\times \\frac{9}{3}\n$$\n\nSo the missing fraction is $\\frac{9}{3}.$" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430668 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430646 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430668 1069 "q-195480" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430668 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430668 1071 "What fraction is missing from the statement below?\n\n$(4÷3)\\times (6÷2)=\\frac{4}{2}\\,\\times $\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430668 1072 #uuid "efe88fd4-c2df-5ce1-afe8-3a63fe72cba4" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430668 1074 "The given expression is\n\n$$\n(4\\,÷\\,3)\\times (6\\,÷\\,2).\n$$\n\nSince our expression contains multiplication and division only, we can write an equivalent expression by swapping the $÷\\,3$ and the $÷\\,2$:\n\n$$\n(4\\,÷\\,2)\\times (6\\,÷\\,3)\n$$\n\nWe can now interpret the divisions as fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{2}\\times \\frac{6}{3}\n$$\n\nSo the missing factor is $\\frac{6}{3}.$" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430669 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430640 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430669 1069 "q-136891" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430669 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430669 1071 "What fraction is missing from the statement below?\n\n$$\n(9÷2)\\times (11÷10)=\\frac{\\boxed{\\,\\,}}{\\boxed{\\,\\,}}\\times \\frac{11}{2}\n$$" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430669 1072 #uuid "f40e1a9a-bc30-5780-acaf-efe9da07376c" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430669 1074 "The given expression is\n\n$$\n(9\\,÷\\,2)\\times (11\\,÷\\,10).\n$$\n\nSince our expression contains multiplication and division only, we can write an equivalent expression by swapping the $÷\\,2$ and the $÷\\,10:$\n\n$$\n(9\\,÷\\,10)\\times (11\\,÷\\,2)\n$$\n\nWe can now interpret the divisions as fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{10}\\times \\frac{11}{2}\n$$\n\nSo the missing fraction is $\\frac{9}{10}.$" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430670 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430636 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430670 1069 "q-211481" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430670 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430670 1071 "Expressed as a fraction in lowest terms, $\\frac{16}{9}\\times \\frac{1}{28}=${{field-1}}." 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430670 1072 #uuid "fceaf763-2a1c-5ef1-b51c-0b12e59864a9" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430670 1074 "We need to solve the following multiplication problem:\n\n$$\n\\frac{16}{9}\\times \\frac{1}{28}\n$$\n\nNotice that the first fraction's numerator ($16$) and the second fraction's denominator ($28$) have a common \nfactor of $4.$ \n\nTherefore, we can simplify our problem by first swapping the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{16}{28}\\times \\frac{1}{9}\n$$\n\nNext, we reduce the first fraction to its lowest terms by dividing the numerator and denominator by $4.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16÷4}{28÷4}\\times \\frac{1}{9} & =\\frac{4}{7}\\times \\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{7}\\times \\frac{1}{9}=\\frac{4\\times 1}{7\\times 9}=\\frac{4}{63}\n$$" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430671 1068 #edb/ref 17592186430644 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430671 1069 "q-61673" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430671 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430671 1071 "$\\frac{4}{5}\\times \\frac{15}{2}=$" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430671 1072 #uuid "fe9d7537-9d25-5842-8fc7-2ece42e6d933" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true] [17592186430671 1074 "Interpreting the fraction as division, we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n(4\\,÷\\,5)\\times (15\\,÷\\,2).\n$$\n\nWe use parentheses to make it easier to read.\n\nSince our expression contains multiplication and division only, we can write an equivalent expression by swapping the $÷\\,5$ and the $÷\\,2$:\n\n$$\n(4\\,÷\\,2)\\times (15\\,÷\\,5)\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the $4÷2$ and $15÷5$ as fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{2}\\times \\frac{15}{5}\n$$" 13194139534640 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-001b2fc4-e19b-55f3-88e4-2e4cc199be37" 17592186430554 "answer-01094c2a-c78c-5ed8-b1d6-1b94eda5d574" 17592186430555 "answer-04459a90-5778-53c3-81a4-feacfd08716f" 17592186430556 "answer-050ee2bc-6a20-543e-9e17-0fd7406a1785" 17592186430557 "answer-07282d48-88bb-5986-812b-b1ad5940eec8" 17592186430558 "answer-0dd3ba50-6268-549b-91c3-d5ecd4bf40ee" 17592186430559 "answer-18184068-8bbe-5aaa-b472-4c1fdc10006e" 17592186430560 "answer-1bbeabb3-4653-56a8-a747-7a2d715f9eb9" 17592186430561 "answer-1cb0afc6-4da0-5c91-9872-0603b7132149" 17592186430562 "answer-27a4114c-4ed1-5603-a522-9bddad77588d" 17592186430563 "answer-2924ec19-dea2-5288-9db4-a9cb6b6ea6a9" 17592186430564 "answer-2b5fe4bf-2ebb-5e56-acfb-f8f740c6496e" 17592186430565 "answer-30e86331-1d09-538f-8117-f3257aababe7" 17592186430566 "answer-38be066b-1060-556f-b0f3-3b2e5b8a2241" 17592186430567 "answer-3bb73056-9bb2-5c81-af79-24007bd492a5" 17592186430568 "answer-3e75fdc9-1404-55dc-9f03-d37732c6be36" 17592186430569 "answer-40ed7987-15fc-5e02-8aef-70ab495d4217" 17592186430570 "answer-41179ec7-a94b-555a-8aaf-935e2fc49a6e" 17592186430571 "answer-41b2e0a9-630b-5e4f-84c0-cfdee9aa2627" 17592186430572 "answer-4392b4d2-2